title: The Cost-of-Living Backlash
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: inflation >= 5.5 and dem_president = 1 and backlash_done != 1 and year >= 2021
priority: 250

= The Cost-of-Living Backlash

Prices are eating into paychecks. Polls show the voters are blaming the party in power. The next election looks grim.

- @backlash_message: Tell voters about the real gains
- @backlash_policy: Pivot to cost-of-living policies
- @backlash_blame: Blame corporate greed

@backlash_message
on-arrival: backlash_done = 1; working_dem -= 1*(1-dissent); dem_enthusiasm -= 0.3

Many voters think we are out of touch.

@backlash_policy
on-arrival: backlash_done = 1; working_dem += 2*(1-dissent); suburban_dem += 1*(1-dissent); populist_strength += 2; budget -= 0

We announce policies on housing, groceries, and healthcare costs.

@backlash_blame
on-arrival: backlash_done = 1; working_dem += 1*(1-dissent); biz_relation -= 4; populist_strength += 2; progressive_dissent -= 2

A populist message resonates with some.
